From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Subject: [PATCH] Declare requires_opengl, because flycast does

The addon declares requires_opengl=false, which reads as a software core. It is
not one. core/libretro/libretro.cpp negotiates Vulkan, then GLES3, then GLES2,
and ends:

    if (!foundRenderApi)
       return false;    // retro_load_game fails outright

There is no software rasteriser in the libretro build and no HAVE_OPENGL=0
switch in its Makefile.

Kodi 22 never reads this field - there is not one reference to requires_opengl
anywhere in xbmc - so this changes no behaviour today. It is corrected because
it is the only machine-readable statement the addon makes about what it needs,
every other core in the repo gets it right, and a frontend that starts honouring
it should hide flycast rather than offer it and fail at load.

--- a/game.libretro.flycast/addon.xml.in
+++ b/game.libretro.flycast/addon.xml.in
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 		<supports_vfs>false</supports_vfs>
 		<supports_standalone>true</supports_standalone>
 		<supports_disc_control>true</supports_disc_control>
-		<requires_opengl>false</requires_opengl>
+		<requires_opengl>true</requires_opengl>
 	</extension>
 	<extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
 		<license>GPLv2</license>
